message: >-
  If you use BioBenchShift, cite the archived release/commit and the
  accompanying peer-reviewed article when available.
title: >-
  BioBenchShift: Benchmark design redirects biomedical discovery
version: pre-submission-2026.09.13
date-released: "2026-09-13"
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Noor
    given-names: Adeeb
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Information Technology, Faculty of Computing and Information
      Technology, King Abdulaziz University, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia
    email: arnoor@kau.edu.sa
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8251-1853"
repository-code: "https://github.com/adeebnoor/BioBenchShift"
url: "https://github.com/adeebnoor/BioBenchShift"
keywords:
  - biomedical artificial intelligence
  - benchmark design
  - model selection
  - hypothesis prioritization
  - network biology
  - drug-target interaction
  - protein-protein interaction
  - structural bias
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  BioBenchShift is the pre-submission reproducibility package for a study
  testing whether biomedical AI benchmark construction changes model selection,
  hypothesis identity, and later or independent evidence concentrated among
  prioritized hypotheses.
